{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>See.</b> Consider carefully." "<b>For YHWH has given you the Sabbath.</b> This is not a commandment alone, but a gift that was not given to any others, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Shabbat 10b): 'I have a good gift in My treasury and its name is Sabbath, and I wish to give it to Israel.' And so they arranged in the prayer: 'You did not give it to the nations of the lands … the uncircumcised,' as it says (Exodus 31:16): וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת הַשַּׁבָּת לְדֹרֹתָם — which is that they should attain the day that is entirely Sabbath."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:55.264677827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}